# Byte-exact checkouts: what is committed is exactly what lands on disk.
#
# Why: runs/SHA256SUMS.txt hashes raw bytes (tools/check_hashes.py). This machine
# has core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a fresh Windows clone would convert
# every text file to CRLF on checkout and the whole manifest would mismatch --
# a "clean machine" run would then look like a failure that is not real.
#
# "* -text" means "never convert, never guess": no CRLF<->LF rewriting in either
# direction. launcher/run.bat is committed with LF and is hashed, so it must not be
# rewritten either. Byte-for-byte is the only thing the manifest can promise.
* -text

# Self-documenting (already implied by "* -text"): these are never text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
*.class binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
